{"ts":"2026-08-09T23:47:48.829Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"f387ff12865a026ff775e35b","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-09T23:47:48.800Z","author":"claude","text":"author=claude,created_at=now,text=The fifteen split into roughly nine docstring-accuracy corrections in filters, graph-canvas, board, crypto, routes/pm, project-watcher, realtime-bus and sse, and six pre-existing code defects the documentation pass exposed: a service worker treating an IndexedDB failure as a drained queue, mutation replay that is not idempotent before retrying accepted requests, a pidfile shutdown not bound to process identity, filesystem errors other than ENOENT being swallowed, and a sweep file list that can change under a multi-tick sweep"}},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-09T23:47:48.800Z","author":"claude","text":"The completed CodeRabbit review returned 18 findings. Three are addressed in commit a40a792: escHtml no longer claims general injection safety,typeIcon escapes its argument before writing it into a title attribute,and the Neo4j driver cache key now covers a SHA-256 digest of the password so a rotation cannot leave the cached driver holding old credentials. Fifteen remain open on the pull request"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-09T23:47:48.829Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-09T23:47:48.800Z","author":"claude","text":"Writing an accurate docstring forces a reading of the body that ordinary review skips,so a documentation pass is an unusually effective bug-finding exercise. The defects it surfaced here were pre-existing and included two security issues,which argues for documenting untouched code rather than only new code"}]}],"before_hash":"e15fa1d4d3cd335b6ae34ef6c7e2ff3660a45de88b6e079f94c291c1b6527955","after_hash":"d75eabbfcc8e459ca26662eefd8e38ef6ad02194de19db6f2d305b377a676992","message":"Record the review findings the documentation pass surfaced"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T07:44:42.730Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"1684e74de48dd9cf0e628b6d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T07:44:42.730Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"The previous symlink test (isMainInvocation resolves a symlinked entry path to the real module URL) passed argv[1] as the link and moduleUrl as the REAL path, which the old one-sided comparison pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl also satisfied — it could not distinguish the fixed implementation from the broken one. Applied the missing canonicalization fix (both sides through realpathSync) and added a new test (canonicalizes a symlinked moduleUrl, as --preserve-symlinks produces) that puts the symlink in moduleUrl (pathToFileURL(link).href), which is what Node records in import.meta.url under --preserve-symlinks. Verified by measurement: reverting to the old one-sided comparison makes the new test fail (fail 1), restoring the canonicalization makes it pass (fail 0). The existing symlink test is retained because argv[1] arriving through an npm bin shim is a separate real case. Note: this repo's gate was on the old broken implementation (branch adopt-canonical-docstring-gate); the canonicalization fix was applied as part of this change."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T07:44:42.730Z"}],"before_hash":"d75eabbfcc8e459ca26662eefd8e38ef6ad02194de19db6f2d305b377a676992","after_hash":"76d669312e73b47b3e55f201fd20d9d26ac991f849e7a064d6f842263c7caff8"}
